```cpp
// File: main.cpp
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    std::cout << "Hello, World!" << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

### Explanation:
* **`#include <iostream>`**: Ye standard input/output library include karta hai taaki hum screen par print (`cout`) kar sakein.
* **`int main()`**: C++ program ka entry point, jahan se execution shuru hoti hai.
* **`std::cout << "Hello, World!"`**: Text ko console par print karne ke liye use hota hai.
* **`std::endl`**: New line insert karta hai aur output buffer flush karta hai.
* **`return 0;`**: Operating system ko batata hai ki program successfully execute ho gaya.

### How to Compile & Run:
```bash
g++ main.cpp -o main
./main
```
